## Good to know

- MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec help MACRO_INLINE_CODE lists every command; MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec help COMMAND MACRO_INLINE_CODE explains one of them.
- A task ID is up to 8 characters long; environment and desk names up to 10.
- MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec add MACRO_INLINE_CODE with no ID makes one up for you: 00000001, 00000002, and so on.
- Most commands fall back to the current environment, desk and task, so
  MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec cat MACRO_INLINE_CODE , MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec set -P high MACRO_INLINE_CODE and MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec rm MACRO_INLINE_CODE all work with no arguments.
- Aliases live in MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec.cfg MACRO_INLINE_CODE : MACRO_INLINE_CODE dir = "ls" MACRO_INLINE_CODE makes MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec dir MACRO_INLINE_CODE run MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec ls MACRO_INLINE_CODE .
- Colors, hooks and debug output can be flipped per run with MACRO_INLINE_CODE -C MACRO_INLINE_CODE , MACRO_INLINE_CODE -H MACRO_INLINE_CODE
  and MACRO_INLINE_CODE -D MACRO_INLINE_CODE , which is handy when a hook misbehaves.

